# .trivyignore — Accepted OS-level CVE suppressions for EMCIP Docker images
#
# PURPOSE
# -------
# This file suppresses known, accepted CVEs that originate from OS-level C libraries
# (OpenSSL/libssl3, zlib, glibc, libstdc++, curl) in the base images used by EMCIP
# services.  These CVEs cannot be remediated by updating Java dependencies; they
# require an upstream base-image update.  They are suppressed here to keep the
# GitHub Security dashboard focused on actionable, Java-level findings.
#
# DO NOT add Java library CVEs to this file.  Only OS/C-library issues belong here.
#
# BASE IMAGES IN SCOPE
# --------------------
#   - eclipse-temurin:21-jre          (JVM services: intent-classifier, moderation-service,
#                                       audit-service, admin-api, admin-ui)
#   - eclipse-temurin:21-jre + libssl3 + zlib1g
#                                      (tdlib-adapter runtime: TDLib requires these system libs)
#   - debian:12-slim                   (native-image services: policy-engine,
#                                       conversation-context, llm-orchestrator)
#
# BUILD-ONLY STAGES (not scanned by Trivy)
#   - ghcr.io/graalvm/native-image-community:25.0.1
#   - eclipse-temurin:21-jdk
#
# HOW TO UPDATE
# -------------
# When a new Trivy scan run produces OS-level CVE IDs not covered here:
#   1. Confirm the affected package is an OS/C library (not a JVM artifact).
#   2. Check whether the CVE has a fix available in debian:12 or ubuntu jammy repos.
#   3. If no upstream fix is available within the pinned base image, add it below
#      with a comment explaining the package, severity, and reason for acceptance.
#   4. Re-run the Trivy scan locally to verify suppression:
#        trivy image --ignorefile .trivyignore <image>
#
# FORMAT: one CVE ID per line, preceded by a comment.
# See: https://aquasecurity.github.io/trivy/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/

# =============================================================================
# OpenSSL / libssl3 / libcrypto3
# =============================================================================
# Present in: all images (debian:12-slim, eclipse-temurin:21-jre via ubuntu:jammy base).
# The TDLib adapter runtime explicitly installs libssl3 as a shared-library
# dependency of libtdjni.so.  The JRE images inherit OpenSSL from Ubuntu Jammy.
# These CVEs are tracked by Debian/Ubuntu security teams; no backport is available
# in the pinned base-image versions.

# CVE-2023-2650: OpenSSL — excessive time spent in OBJ_obj2txt() with large OIDs
# Affects: openssl/libssl3 in debian:12 / ubuntu:jammy before 3.0.9
# Acceptance: no EMCIP code calls OBJ_obj2txt(); exposure is through TLS handshake
# only.  Fix requires base image rebuild with openssl >= 3.0.9.
CVE-2023-2650

# CVE-2023-3446: OpenSSL — excessive time in DH_check() / DH_check_pub_key()
# Affects: openssl/libssl3 in debian:12 / ubuntu:jammy
# Acceptance: EMCIP does not use raw DH key material; exposure is theoretical.
CVE-2023-3446

# CVE-2023-3817: OpenSSL — excessive time in DH_check_pub_key() with large q param
# Affects: openssl/libssl3; follow-on to CVE-2023-3446
# Acceptance: same rationale as CVE-2023-3446 above.
CVE-2023-3817

# CVE-2023-5678: OpenSSL — excessive time in DH key/parameter generation
# Affects: openssl/libssl3 in debian:12
# Acceptance: EMCIP does not generate DH keys at runtime.
CVE-2023-5678

# CVE-2024-0727: OpenSSL — null-pointer dereference when parsing a malformed PKCS12 file
# Affects: openssl/libssl3 in debian:12-slim / ubuntu:jammy
# Acceptance: EMCIP does not parse untrusted PKCS12 files.
CVE-2024-0727

# CVE-2024-2511: OpenSSL — unbounded memory growth with session handling in TLSv1.3
# Affects: openssl/libssl3 in debian:12 before 3.0.14
# Acceptance: internal service-to-service TLS only; sessions are short-lived.
CVE-2024-2511

# CVE-2024-4603: OpenSSL — excessive time checking DSA keys and parameters
# Affects: openssl/libssl3 in debian:12
# Acceptance: EMCIP uses RSA/ECDSA only, not DSA.
CVE-2024-4603

# CVE-2024-5535: OpenSSL — SSL_select_next_proto buffer overread
# Affects: openssl/libssl3 in debian:12 before 3.0.14
# Acceptance: application-layer ALPN selection is handled by the JVM/Netty stack,
# not the OS libssl.
CVE-2024-5535

# =============================================================================
# zlib / zlib1g
# =============================================================================
# Present in: eclipse-temurin:21-jre (ubuntu:jammy), tdlib-adapter runtime
# (explicitly installed).  TDLib requires zlib1g as a build and runtime dep.

# CVE-2023-45853: zlib — integer overflow in zipOpenNewFileInZip4_64
# Affects: zlib/zlib1g in ubuntu:jammy, debian:12 before 1:1.2.11.dfsg-4
# Acceptance: EMCIP does not use zlib's zip-writing API; Kafka and Spring
# compression go through the JVM's java.util.zip which is unaffected.
CVE-2023-45853

# =============================================================================
# glibc / libc6
# =============================================================================
# Present in: all images.  glibc in debian:12 and ubuntu:jammy carries several
# low-severity issues with no available backport at the pinned image versions.

# CVE-2023-4806: glibc — potential use-after-free in getaddrinfo()
# Affects: glibc/libc6 in debian:12 / ubuntu:jammy
# Acceptance: no fix available in the pinned base images; DNS resolution is
# handled by the JVM's JNDI stack, not direct glibc getaddrinfo() calls from
# application code.
CVE-2023-4806

# CVE-2023-4813: glibc — potential use-after-free in gaih_inet()
# Affects: glibc/libc6 in debian:12 / ubuntu:jammy
# Acceptance: companion to CVE-2023-4806; same rationale.
CVE-2023-4813

# CVE-2023-5156: glibc — memory leak in getaddrinfo() with AF_UNSPEC
# Affects: glibc/libc6 in debian:12 / ubuntu:jammy
# Acceptance: short-lived DNS queries; memory leak impact is negligible.
CVE-2023-5156

# CVE-2024-2961: glibc — buffer overflow in iconv() with ISO-2022-CN-EXT
# Affects: glibc/libc6 in debian:12 before 2.36-9+deb12u7
# Acceptance: EMCIP does not invoke iconv() with ISO-2022-CN-EXT encoding.
CVE-2024-2961

# CVE-2024-33599: glibc — stack-based buffer overflow in netgroup cache
# Affects: glibc/libc6 in debian:12 / ubuntu:jammy
# Acceptance: nscd (name service cache daemon) is not running in any EMCIP container.
CVE-2024-33599

# CVE-2024-33600: glibc — null pointer dereference in netgroup cache
# Affects: glibc/libc6; companion to CVE-2024-33599
# Acceptance: same rationale; nscd not present in containers.
CVE-2024-33600

# CVE-2024-33601: glibc — netgroup cache may terminate daemon on memory allocation failure
# Affects: glibc/libc6; companion to CVE-2024-33599
# Acceptance: same rationale; nscd not present in containers.
CVE-2024-33601

# CVE-2024-33602: glibc — netgroup cache relies on undefined behaviour
# Affects: glibc/libc6; companion to CVE-2024-33599
# Acceptance: same rationale; nscd not present in containers.
CVE-2024-33602

# =============================================================================
# libstdc++6 / gcc runtime
# =============================================================================
# Present in: eclipse-temurin:21-jre (ubuntu:jammy).
# The GCC runtime libraries pulled transitively into the JRE image occasionally
# carry advisory-level CVEs that have no exploitable path through Java code.

# CVE-2023-4039: GCC — incorrect stack protector for C99 VLAs on aarch64
# Affects: gcc-12/libstdc++6 in ubuntu:jammy on arm64
# Acceptance: EMCIP Java code does not use C99 VLAs; this only affects
# C/C++ binaries compiled with the affected gcc-12 version.
CVE-2023-4039

# =============================================================================
# curl / libcurl4
# =============================================================================
# curl is installed in all images for the Docker HEALTHCHECK command only.
# It is not used as an application library.

# CVE-2023-38545: curl — SOCKS5 heap buffer overflow
# Affects: curl in ubuntu:jammy / debian:12 before 8.4.0
# Acceptance: curl is used only for the /actuator/health HEALTHCHECK probe
# against localhost; it does not connect to external SOCKS5 proxies.
CVE-2023-38545

# CVE-2023-38546: curl — cookie injection with none file
# Affects: curl in ubuntu:jammy / debian:12 before 8.4.0
# Acceptance: healthcheck curl invocation uses no cookies or SOCKS proxies.
CVE-2023-38546

# CVE-2024-2398: curl — HTTP/2 push headers memory leak
# Affects: curl/libcurl4 in debian:12 before 8.7.1
# Acceptance: healthcheck does not use HTTP/2 server push.
CVE-2024-2398

# CVE-2024-7264: curl — ASN.1 date parser out-of-bounds read
# Affects: curl/libcurl4 in debian:12
# Acceptance: healthcheck connects only to localhost; no untrusted certificates.
CVE-2024-7264

# =============================================================================
# TDLib build-stage dependencies (emcip-tdlib-adapter only)
# =============================================================================
# The tdlib-adapter Dockerfile Stage 1 (eclipse-temurin:21-jdk AS tdlib-builder)
# installs cmake, g++, libssl-dev, zlib1g-dev, gperf via apt to compile TDLib.
# Trivy scans only the final runtime image (Stage 3), so build-stage packages are
# not scanned.  The entries below cover the Stage 3 runtime image which explicitly
# installs libssl3 and zlib1g for the libtdjni.so shared library.
#
# All OpenSSL and zlib entries above already cover the tdlib-adapter runtime.
# No additional suppressions are needed specifically for the TDLib runtime image.
